WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.710
Labradors come in three coats:
black, chocolate and yellow.

2
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.880
Two black Labradors can
have a yellow puppy.

3
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:13.150
One gene, called B, decides whether
the dark pigment is black or brown.

4
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.490
Yet a yellow dog shows neither.

5
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:20.320
So how can one gene decide whether
another gene gets any say at all?

6
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:25.200
In this mission, you'll cross two black
Labradors on a 16-cell grid and predict

7
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:29.440
the puppies: 9 black,
3 chocolate, 4 yellow.

8
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.320
Then you'll sort squash
plants by their fruit,

9
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:37.080
white, yellow or green, and find
the ratio hidden in the counts.

10
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:42.530
Your mission: explain how one gene can
decide whether another gene gets any say.
